{"text": "MEMORANDUM\n\nLEGISLATIVE REFERENCE BUREAU\n\nWWW.MILWAUKEE.GOVILRB\n\nAld Robert G. Donovan\n\nDana J. Zelazny, Legislative Reference Bureau\nDate: January 30, 2018\nSubject: \u2014 PAUL NANNIS/STRATEGIC HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC\n\nThis memo was prepared in response to your request of January 29, 2018, for details of\nany work Mr. Paul Nannis may have undertaken on behalf of the Health Department\n(MHD) during former Commissioner Bevan Baker's term of service (2004-2018).\n\nContracts Awarded to Strategic Healthcare Solutions, LLC\n\nMr. Nannis is the owner of Strategic Healthcare Solutions, LLC. Since 2009, Mr.\nNannis's company has held various contracts with the Health Department to provide\nconsultation services. The total value of the contracts awarded by the Health\nDepartment to Mr. Nannis's company from 2004-2018 is $514,863\n\nThe table on page 2 summarizes the contracts awarded to Mr. Nannis's company from\n2004-2018, including the value of the contract, the hourly rate (if specified in the\ncontract), and the services provided.\n\nPayments to Mr. Nannis and Strategic Healthcare Solutions, LLC\n\nThe attached spreadsheet shows the actual payments made by the City to Mr. Nannis\nand his company, Strategic Healthcare Solutions, LLC. Payments begin in 2008 and\ncontinue through 2016, totaling $556,788 (including $4,988 in reimbursements for\nexpenses, primarily travel-related). Payments under columns that start with \u201cGR\" are\ngrant-funded.\n\nLead-Related Services\nNone of the contracts identified by the Department of Administration - Purchasing\n\nDivision as having been awarded to Mr. Nannis or his company require services on\nlead-related issues or include any reference to MHD's lead-related programs.\n\nIf you have any other question related to this matter, please let me know.\n\nLRB 170742",
